\label{def:dcd}
The Delay Complexity Dimension of $(\mathcal{H},P,W)$ is
$\mathrm{DCD}(\mathcal{H},P,W) := d/\eta(W)$.

\label{lem:quantize}
For any $M\ge 2$ there is a deterministic quantizer $f_M$ such that
$I(Y;f_M(D\wedge W)\mid X)\ge I_W$.

\label{thm:info-tradeoff}
Under Assumption~\ref{ass:oracle}, ERM on $\mathcal{H}'$ with pseudo-labels
$\hat Y(X,Q_M)$ achieves, with probability at least $1-\delta$,
\begin{multline*}
R(\hat h_M)-\inf_{h\in\mathcal{H}}R(h)\\
\le C_1\sqrt{\tfrac{d/q(W)+\log(1/\delta)}{n}}
+C_2\sqrt{\tfrac{H(Y\!\mid\!X)-I(Y;Q_M\!\mid\!X)}{n}}
\end{multline*}
up to logarithmic factors. The bound is monotone improving in the
partition: $I(Y;Q_M\mid X)\ge I_W$ for every $M\ge 2$, and refining
$f_M$ never decreases it (Lemma~\ref{lem:quantize}).
